12
00:47:00,000 --> 00:47:06,000
Trainspotting is a 1996 British crime black comedy drama film directed by Danny Boyle, and starring Ewan McGregor,
Ewen Bremner, Jonny Lee Miller, Kevin McKidd, Robert Carlyle and Kelly Macdonald in her film debut.

13
00:50:55,000 --> 00:51:01,000
It is written in English and Scots.

14
00:54:50,000 --> 00:54:56,000
Based on the 1993 novel by Irvine Welsh, the film was
released in the United Kingdom on 23 February 1996.

15
00:58:45,000 --> 00:58:51,000
The film follows a group of heroin addicts in an economically
depressed area of Edinburgh and their passage through life.

16
01:02:40,000 --> 01:02:46,000
Beyond drug addiction, other themes in the film include an
exploration of urban poverty and squalor in Edinburgh.

17
01:06:35,000 --> 01:06:41,000
Trainspotting was released to critical acclaim, and is regarded by
many critics as one of the best films of the 1990s.

18
01:10:30,000 --> 01:10:36,000
The film was ranked tenth by the British Film Institute (BFI) in its
list of Top 100 British films of the 20th century.

19
01:14:25,000 --> 01:14:31,000
In 2004, the film was voted the best Scottish film of
all time in a general public poll.

20
01:18:20,000 --> 01:18:26,000
A 2017 poll, which consisted of 150 actors, directors, writers, producers and critics
for Time Out magazine, ranked it the tenth best British film ever.

21
01:22:15,000 --> 01:22:21,000
A sequel, T2 Trainspotting, was released in January 2017,
with TriStar Pictures distributing it.

